expected_issues.description:
Potential namespace/qualification regression: the old code assigned to `Base::PyExc_*` globals, but the new code assigns to unqualified `PyExc_FC_*`. If these variables live in `Base::` (as before), this will either fail to compile or silently assign different symbols (if there are similarly named globals in another namespace). Suggest explicitly qualifying (e.g., `Base::PyExc_FC_GeneralError = ...`) or adding `using Base::PyExc_FC_GeneralError;` etc. Also consider making `module` a `PyObject* const` or capturing by value to avoid referencing a local through the lambda unnecessarily.

```suggestion
    Base::PyExc_FC_GeneralError = setup("FreeCADError", PyExc_RuntimeError);
    Base::PyExc_FC_FreeCADAbort = setup("FreeCADAbort", PyExc_BaseException);
    Base::PyExc_FC_XMLBaseException = setup("XMLBaseException", PyExc_Exception);
```

